+// Is the local player loading their weapons by hand?
+//
+// The server answers this from the player's userinfo. Prediction only ever
+// runs for the LOCAL player, whose answer is simply the cvar that populates
+// that userinfo in the first place - so the two agree by construction.
+//
+// It has to exist here at all because GoldSrc compiles the weapon code twice,
+// once for the server and once for client-side prediction. A guard present in
+// one and absent in the other is a weapon that behaves differently depending
+// on who is asking, which is the classic source of prediction glitches.
+// The magazine leaves the weapon, predicted the same way the server does it.
+//
+// GoldSrc compiles the weapon classes twice, so a body that exists only on
+// the server is a link error here and a prediction mismatch if it were left
+// hollow. The rounds are lost on both sides or neither.
+void CBasePlayerWeapon::DropMagazine( void )
+{
+	if( m_iClip <= 0 )
+		return;
+
+	// One stays in the chamber; the rest go with the magazine.
+	m_iClip = ( m_iClip > 0 ) ? 1 : 0;
+}
+
+BOOL UTIL_PlayerHandLoads( CBaseEntity *pPlayer )
+{
+	return ( gEngfuncs.pfnGetCvarFloat( "vr_handload" ) != 0.0f ) ? TRUE : FALSE;
+}
